fnm for Debian/Ubuntu
=====================

fnm needs a line in the shell's startup file to put its Node.js versions
on PATH:

  eval "$(fnm env)"                # bash/zsh
  fnm env | source                 # fish

Add --use-on-cd to switch versions automatically when entering a
directory with a .nvmrc, .node-version or package.json engines field.

Versions install under $FNM_DIR (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/fnm, usually
~/.local/share/fnm) with "fnm install <version>" or "fnm install --lts".
Downloads come from https://nodejs.org/dist (override with
FNM_NODE_DIST_MIRROR), so installing versions needs network access and
the ca-certificates package.

Bash, zsh and fish completions are installed system-wide; they were
generated by "fnm completions" at build time.

